        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Kansas City Power & Light District\n- Companies: H&R Block\n- Projects: Midland Theatre renovation\n- Products: Alamo Drafthouse Mainstreet Cinema\n- Topics: mixed-use development, tax preparation\n\nFacts:\n- The Kansas City Power & Light District is an $850 million mixed-use district.\n- The Kansas City Power & Light District is one of the largest development projects in the Midwestern United States.\n- The Kansas City Power & Light District is anchored by the renovated Midland Theatre.\n- The Kansas City Power & Light District is anchored by Alamo Drafthouse Mainstreet Cinema.\n- The Kansas City Power & Light District is anchored by the world headquarters of H&R Block.\n- H&R Block is an American tax preparation company.\n- H&R Block operates in North America, Australia, and India.",
